<div class="side-by-side">
  <p class="big">Invitational: risk, reward and a blind offer</p>
  <p>
    Ten teams of three, each pairing a COD: Mobile creator with a mobile FPS
    creator and a non-endemic PC creator, competed for a $50K prize pool in a
    loot race format. After each round, teams bid DMZ Cash for a share of the
    pool. Bidding meant risk. Not bidding meant giving up cash for a long-term
    edge. The offers were blind, so no team could copy another. In one round, a
    bid just $1 higher than a rival’s was worth an extra $1,000.
  </p>
</div>

